@Akotski-ys9rr you sound no fun. Also traction control is not needed. What do you happend with cars before [PLATE REDACTED]'s? There was no traction control then, and people were still driving lambos and such. Driving without tractoin control is not hard. Its not much different. 

Traction control sorta limits the throttle response when losing grip. This is why people often disable it when the car is stuck in snow, since it will just not give enough throttle to get out of the snow, since it will start limiting it.

Traction control is only needed in heavy thunderstorms or heavy snowstorms
